   "notes": "Bene't Street (south-facing) side of 1 King's Parade, seen only at grazing angles from Bene't Street (Mapillary 196026592363155, 385248065955225, 963912667759231). Painted white brick/render, 4 storeys of small-paned (6/6) sashes, parapet. West end (x=0) has the dark iron-and-glass Cambridge Chop House front wrapping round from the corner (rest of it is wall :0); a white panelled door near the east end just west of the downpipe and the ashlar of 9 Bene't St (the stone wall with the 'PH' hanging sign belongs to 9 Bene't St, not to this wall). Bay count (3 per floor) and ground-floor window/door positions are estimates."
